d Prevention, National Center for Health Statistics</collab></person-group><article-title>United States Life Tables 2002</article-title><source>CDC National Center for Health Statistics: National Vital Statistics Reports</source><volume>53</volume><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/nchs/data/dvs/life2002.pdf"/><comment>Accessed January 14, 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Statistics Canada</collab></person-group><article-title>Duchesne D. Life tables, Canada, provinces and territories, 1995&#x02013;1997</article-title><source>Statistics Canada, Summary Tables</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.statcan.ca/english/freepub/84-537-XIE/84-537-XIE1997001.htm"/><comment>Accessed January 14, 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organization</collab></person-group><article-title>WHO-UNICEF estimates of BCG coverage</article-title><source>WHO, Immunization, surveillance, assessment &#x00026; monitoring</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/immunization_monitoring/en/globalsummary/timeseries/tswucoveragebcg.htm"/><comment>Accessed January 14, 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Menzies</surname><given-names>RI</given-names></name><name><surname>Vissandjee</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of Bacille Calmette-Guerin vaccination on tuberculin reactivity</article-title><source>Am Rev Respir Dis</source><year>1992</year><volume>145</volume><fpage>621</fpage><lpage>625</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1546843</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Farhat</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenaway</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pai</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Menzies</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>False positive tuberculin tests: what is the absolute effect of BCG and non-tuberculous mycobacteria</article-title><source>Int J Tuberc Lung Dis</source><year>2006</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>1192</fpage><lpage>1204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17131776</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salpeter</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name><name><surname>Salpeter</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mathematical model for the epidemiology of tuberculosis, with estimates of the reproductive number and infection-delay function</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>147</volume><fpage>398</fpage><lpage>406</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9508108</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Behr</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Warren</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Salamon</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopewell</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ponce de</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Daley</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Transmission of Mycobacterium tuberculosis from patients smear-negative for acid-fast bacilli</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1999</year><volume>353</volume><fpage>444</fpage><lpage>449</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9989714</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(98)03406-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mubareka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Perrault</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rocher</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Menzies</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartzman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tuberculosis diagnosed by active vs. passive case-finding</article-title><source>Am J Respir Crit Care Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>163</volume><fpage>A100</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schwartzman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Menzies</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tuberculosis screening of immigrants to low-prevalence countries. A cost-effectiveness analysis</article-title><source>Am J Respir Crit Care Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>161</volume><fpage>780</fpage><lpage>789</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10712322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schechter</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Rose</surname><given-names>DN</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahs</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Silver</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tuberculin screening: cost-effectiveness analysis of various testing schedules</article-title><source>Am J Prev Med</source><year>1990</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2118787</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mohle-Boetani</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given